<title>USA: Granite State ends repurchase program. [CORRECTED 18:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Granite State ends repurchase program. [CORRECTED 18:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>KEENE, New Hampshire 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Granite State Bankshares Inc on Wednesday said it terminated its year-old stock repurchase program after buying (corrects from selling) 72,549 shares.</p>
<p>In a statement, Granite said it terminated the program, authorized on August 13, 1996, in connection with the company's proposed acquisition of Primary Bank.</p>
<p>The merger would take the form of a stock swap, forming a bank with $807 million in assets, Granite said.</p>
